{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and Amplitude’s limits:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let amplitude = try HTTPDestination.amplitude(","    apiKey: apiKey,","    region: .eu,  \/\/ or .us, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is a JSON object of content type ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"text":" with two members: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"api_key"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"project’s API key, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"text":", one object per record, oldest first, with these members:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"device_id","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" when its context has no session"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event_properties"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s stored properties, by name","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"event_type","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"type":"text","text":", as it is"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert_id"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The session’s start in Unix milliseconds, the first 48 bits of its version 7 ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"text":"; left out for a record with no session, or a session key of another version","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the event was tracked, in whole milliseconds since 1970","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"type":"text","text":", and no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"idfv"},{"type":"text","text":" or other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"device identifier. Amplitude counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"type":"text","text":", so its unique users are sessions. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"type":"text","text":") is its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anonymous user, linked to nothing: Amplitude rejects an event with neither a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"type":"text","text":" nor a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"type":"text","text":". Amplitude drops a second copy of an event with the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record a store recovers after a relaunch keeps its session, so it goes out with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":" of its first send, and Amplitude drops it if it had already stored"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it before the app ended. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s vendor identifier and trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent. Nor is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":": neither an address nor "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$remote"},{"type":"text","text":", which asks Amplitude to look the user’s location up"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the request’s address."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, an element of an array is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Amplitude limits each string value to 1,024 characters; the encoder sends longer ones as they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event also holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"app_version","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The version, left out when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"device_model","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The model","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"language"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"},{"text":", which Amplitude stores as the language’s name","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"platform"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os_name"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os_version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The operating system’s name, its name again, and its version"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name Amplitude keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for its own events, one whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose timestamp has no epoch-milliseconds form, and one too large for a request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":"). "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports on its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. Amplitude answers a request it takes with 200, so "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" retries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one that gets no response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one it rejects, such as with 400 or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"413. A record sent again keeps its "},{"code":"insert_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The bytes are the same for the same records on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/init(apiKey:plan:limit:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/Failure"],"anchor":"Type-Aliases","generated":true,"title":"Type Aliases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/transientStatuses"],"anchor":"Type-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Type Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for: